{"name":"Daly Waters","hex":"#afdadf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"waters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of water","Amniotic fluid ."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of water"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waters"}],"entries":[{"title":"Daly Waters, Northern Territory","blocks":[{"text":"Daly Waters is a town and locality in the Northern Territory of Australia, located about 620 kilometres (390 mi) south of the territory capital of Darwin at the intersection of the Carpentaria Highway and the Stuart Highway. In the 2021 census, the locality of Daly Waters had a population of 55 people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Daly_Waters_Pub_Outside.JPG/330px-Daly_Waters_Pub_Outside.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daly_Waters%2C_Northern_Territory"},{"title":"Daly Waters Airfield","blocks":[{"text":"The Daly Waters Airfield, also RAAF Base Daly Waters, is a former commercial and sporadically-used military airfield located at Daly Waters, Northern Territory, Australia. As an airfield on Australia's earliest international routes, Daly Waters was used throughout the 1920s and 1930s as a stop over for commercial airlines operating on the domestic route to Western Australia and international carriers flying from Australia into south-east Asia via Darwin. During World War II, the airbase was used by the Royal Australian Air Force (RAAF) and the United States Army Air Force to undertake combat operations against the Japanese in New Guinea, the Dutch East Indies and the islands to Australia's north. Following the war, the airbase was used commercially again up until the 1970s when the airfield was sporadically-used by the RAAF."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daly_Waters_Airfield"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Daly-waters-traffic-light-northern-territory-australia.jpg/250px-Daly-waters-traffic-light-northern-territory-australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Daly-waters-traffic-light-northern-territory-australia.jpg/500px-Daly-waters-traffic-light-northern-territory-australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Daly-waters-traffic-light-northern-territory-australia.jpg/250px-Daly-waters-traffic-light-northern-territory-australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaly-waters-traffic-light-northern-territory-australia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Horses_and_carriage.jpg/250px-Horses_and_carriage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/Horses_and_carriage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Horses_and_carriage.jpg/250px-Horses_and_carriage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorses_and_carriage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Daly_Waters_Telegraph_Station.jpeg/250px-Daly_Waters_Telegraph_Station.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Daly_Waters_Telegraph_Station.jpeg/500px-Daly_Waters_Telegraph_Station.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Daly_Waters_Telegraph_Station.jpeg/250px-Da